@title After-Hours Care Options
@subtitle Larch Valley Medical Group, partners' meeting 2026-11-04
@author Odette Rousseau, Practice Manager
@date 2026-11-04

We want to add after-hours care for our 38000 patients.

!!! Decision needed on 2026-11-04: approve the $260000 telehealth budget.

## Options

grid 3

### Extended clinic hours until 21:00
- Annual cost: $410000
- About 900 visits a month
- Average wait: 25 minutes
- Handles any visit that needs an exam

### Telehealth urgent care
**Recommended to start now.**
- Annual cost: $260000
- About 1500 visits a month
- Average wait: 12 minutes
- Cannot handle visits that need a physical exam

### Nurse triage phone line
Open 17:00 to 23:00.
- Annual cost: $185000
- About 2200 calls a month
- Answered within 3 minutes
- Vendor estimates it avoids 18% of emergency room referrals

## Cost per contact

data cpc = option,dollars per contact; Extended hours,38; Telehealth,14; Triage line,7

chart hbar cpc unit=$ labels title="Cost per contact"

## What each can and cannot do

table = Option,Can do,Cannot do; Extended hours,Any visit that needs an exam,Lowest volume and longest wait; Telehealth,Fast access for about 1500 visits a month,Visits that need a physical exam; Triage line,Answers within 3 minutes and may avoid 18% of ER referrals,Treat patients

Extended hours is the most expensive per contact, but it is the only option that treats patients who need an exam. It stays under consideration if telehealth use is low.

## Recommendation

Start with the **telehealth service** now and add the **nurse line** in the second half of 2027.
